**A method and apparatus for the management of communications of a moving platform,** comprising a plurality of platform applications, a communications system configured to transmit data received from the at least one platform application and to effect wireless data communication by means of one of a plurality of supported communication links, and a data management module, wherein the apparatus and method are configured to:

- receive performance data indicative of a current available bandwidth of the, or each, communications link allocated to, or associated with, the platform applications;

- identify, for each platform application, the data to be transmitted thereby to a recipient node, and compare a bandwidth requirement of said data with a current available bandwidth of the respective communications link allocated thereto, or associated therewith;

- in the event that, as a result of said comparison, a current available bandwidth of a communications link is determined to be insufficient in relation to the bandwidth requirement of a specified platform application, generate information data and transmit said information data to the specified platform application, or to a quality of service interface associated therewith; and

- adapt, by means of the specified platform application, or the quality of service interface associated therewith, and upon receipt of the information data, at least one parameter of its respective application data to the current available bandwidth of its respective communications link for transmission to a recipient node.

outputs.L2:
A system and technique for controlling the communications of a mobile platform that includes several platform applications, along with a communications system arranged to send data obtained from the at least one platform application and to carry out wireless data exchange using one among multiple supported communication links, together with a data management module. This apparatus and technique are designed to:

Obtain performance information reflecting the currently available bandwidth of the communications link—or each such link—that is assigned to or connected with the platform applications;

Determine, for every platform application, which data it needs to send to a receiving node, and evaluate the bandwidth demand of that outgoing data against the bandwidth currently available on the corresponding communications link assigned to or linked with that application;

Should this evaluation reveal that a communications link's presently available bandwidth falls short of what a particular platform application requires, produce information data and send it to that particular platform application or to a quality of service interface connected with it;

Once the information data arrives, have the particular platform application—or its associated quality of service interface—modify at least one characteristic of its own application data to match the presently available bandwidth of its corresponding communications link, so that the data can be sent to a receiving node.

