# Independent Claim for Bandwidth Management Invention

**Claim 1.** A system for managing bandwidth across multiple communication links on a vehicle, the system comprising:

a plurality of communication links, each communication link configured to transmit and receive data between the vehicle and one or more external networks, wherein each communication link is associated with a respective set of link characteristics including at least available bandwidth, latency, and cost;

a plurality of onboard applications, each onboard application executing on the vehicle and generating a respective data traffic flow having one or more traffic requirements;

a memory storing a set of policies defining allocation rules for distributing the data traffic flows across the plurality of communication links; and

a bandwidth management controller communicatively coupled to the plurality of communication links and the plurality of onboard applications, the bandwidth management controller configured to:

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;monitor, in real time, the respective set of link characteristics for each of the plurality of communication links;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;determine, for each of the data traffic flows, the one or more traffic requirements;

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;dynamically allocate each of the data traffic flows to at least one of the plurality of communication links based on the monitored set of link characteristics, the determined traffic requirements, and the set of policies; and

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;reallocate at least one of the data traffic flows from a first communication link to a second communication link in response to a detected change in the set of link characteristics of the first communication link.

---

*Note: This claim is drafted broadly to capture the core inventive concept. Depending on the specific novel features of your invention, you may wish to refine the recited elements (e.g., specifying particular allocation algorithms, prioritization schemes, aircraft-specific link types such as SATCOM/ATG/Wi-Fi, or handling of failover conditions). I recommend having a registered patent attorney or agent review and tailor the claim scope in light of the prior art.*
